  "components": [
    {
      "id": "wcb-hcr",
      "name": "WCB · HCR Vocalizer",
      "kind": "wcb-verb",
      "confidence": "high",
      "firmware": "WCB 6.2.1_021242RSEP2026",
      "routing": {
        "class": "wcb-verb",
        "notes": "Needs a WCB with the HCR Vocalizer configured (?HCR,PORT,S<port>:<baud>). On WCB 6.2.1 ;H runs on the board that hosts the HCR: this board if it has one, else the stored ?HCR,REMOTE,W<n> host, else an online board that advertises HCR over WDP (WCB.ino:6391-6409, 6429-6431). A ;H that arrived over the mesh runs where it lands and is never forwarded again. WCB 6.1.x runs ;H only on the board that receives it (6.1.5 WCB.ino:4711-4712); prefix ;W<n>, to reach another board. Needs 6.2+: Set Volume for all channels (;H,VOL,<level>, WCB_HCR.cpp:365-388; 6.1.5 requires a channel) and FN codes 7, 10, 13, 18 and 19. TRIGGER and the all-channel VOLUP/VOLDN step also work on 6.1.5. FN codes follow WcbCmd HcrCodec::normalize (WcbHcr.cpp:7-36; 12 and 15 are rejected); chan runs to 99 for fn 7 (muse gap), track to 9999 for fn 14 (Play WAV). Volume levels are accepted as 0-100, but 6.2.1 sends at most 99 to the HCR (hcrSetVol, WCB_HCR.cpp:84-87)."
      },
